// Laplace_pressure of a droplet around a FROZEN CORE (28 Oct 2026). An
// oil droplet ((O)20, chi 1.2, theta 20000) is nucleated on a frozen X
// core (layers 1-4) of a 40-layer sphere, released, and its theta then
// searched for Laplace_pressure = 0.012.
// Before the fix the kal column read omega at the FROZEN first layer
// (omega = 0 there), so it printed ~1e-16 for every cored droplet, and a
// Laplace_pressure search accepted its first probe. Now a frozen end is
// read at the bulk plateau past it (System._laplace_sites; a one-time note
// names the site).
// Checked at creation (28 Oct 2026): row 2 = 1.16996e-2 = -omega at the
// plateau site x = 11.5, equal to the Flory-Huggins pressure difference
// Pi(phi_in) - Pi(phi_out) of the plateau and far-field compositions
// (0.7597968 / 2.714e-4) to 5e-5 relative (the plateau is flat to 4e-5);
// the coreless twin prints 1.21771e-2 (R_e 18.42 vs 19.58 here: gamma =
// dp R_e/2 = 0.1121 vs 0.1146, the 2 % expected from R_e vs R_s and the
// curvature corrections). Row 3: the search converges to dp = 0.012 in 11
// probes (theta 28754.6). Row 1 (pinned) is the plateau of the pinned
// state. The thin shell with no plateau (NiN, and a search that raises)
// is guarded in tests/input_guards.py. DELIBERATE deviation from Namics
// (oracle 3e9eafd, 28 Oct 2026, starts 1-2): its
// grand_potential_density profile equals ours (6e-9 at the plateau site)
// but it prints Laplace_pressure = -0 for both rows (-omega at the frozen
// layer, system.cpp:1530), and its Laplace_pressure search error
// (system.cpp:1436) reads the same frozen layer.
lat : NN : geometry : spherical
lat : NN : n_layers : 40
lat : NN : lowerbound : mirror
mon : X : freedom : frozen
mon : X : frozen_range : 1;4
mon : O : freedom : pinned
mon : O : pinned_range : 5;20
mon : W : freedom : free
mon : O : chi_W : 1.2
mol : oil : composition : (O)20
mol : oil : freedom : restricted
mol : oil : theta : 20000
mol : W : composition : (W)1
mol : W : freedom : solvent
newton : n : tolerance : 1e-9
output : kal : append : false
kal : mol : oil : theta
kal : sys : NN : Laplace_pressure
kal : sys : NN : grand_potential
output : pro : append : false
pro : sys : NN : grand_potential_density
pro : mol : oil : phi

start

mon : O : freedom : free

start

var : mol-oil : search : theta
var : sys-NN : Laplace_pressure : 0.012

start
